  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Skills, Employment, and Empowerment for the Development of Youth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP South Sudan will use TRAC 2 funds to consolidate peace, stabilize the economy, and build resilience through the adoption and scaling-up of transformative technologies and approaches to transition and recover local economies and improve the well-being of vulnerable youth and women. The initiative will foster employability and livelihood of at least 1,300 youth and women-headed households by matching industry needs with the available skills, transforming key productive value chains to exploit market opportunities in the African Continental Free Trade Area (AfCFTA), and generate income, employment, and livelihood for vulnerable population. The project will pursue the realization of the following key results;</narrative>
  </description>
